Me (self-hosted home computer) authenticates paired phones with opaque
ht1_* session tokens and maps each owner 1:1 to an upstream BetterAuth
user server-side. The private upstream listener is unreachable from
phones directly; the home server forwards native REST calls with a
short-lived, single-use HMAC assertion (x-me-home-assertion, key
ME_HOME_BRIDGE_SECRET, held server-side on both hosts, never sent to
phones).

This patch consumes the assertion at the single AuthService seam:
  - wrapAuthWithHomeBridge(auth) checks the assertion header first and
    returns a { user: { id, email, name, role } } session for it;
  - no assertion header -> pure delegation to BetterAuth/Entra/
    organization sessions (zero behaviour change);
  - no wrapped service (bridge-only: no separate Google/Entra/Okta app)
    -> minimal AuthService declining interactive sign-in, bridge-only
    sessions; with no bridge key the bridge path always refuses;
  - present-but-invalid assertion -> null (refuse; never fall through).
  - role travels inside the signed assertion per request (no cache), so
    operator role changes apply on the next call; no BetterAuth rows are
    created (virtual trusted principal); unique stable home-mapped ids.
  - nonce + 60s TTL: each assertion is accepted exactly once (replay
    refused via a bounded in-memory seen-cache).

Same-request re-reads (P0-2 fix, rev3): native request-actor
identifyUser AND identifyActor and guards may read the SAME HTTP request
multiple times. The wrapper memoizes the verified identity PER ACTUAL
REQUEST HEADERS OBJECT (WeakMap) bound to the assertion value, so
re-reading auth within the same Request succeeds without re-consuming
the nonce. A NEW Request / new Headers object reusing an assertion
replays and is refused. Mutated headers invalidate the cache and refuse
(never fall through to cookies). Raw verifyHomeAssertion still denies
replay on every call; the one-time nonce guard is not disabled globally
and no shared admin is accepted.

Bridge-only boot (P0-1 fix, rev3): readConfig.singleUser previously
threw without Google/Microsoft/Okta even with a valid bridge key, before
the index wrap ran. config.ts now recognises a valid dedicated
ME_HOME_BRIDGE_SECRET (>=32 chars) as an auth authority: with a valid
key and no external OAuth, full loadConfig returns singleUser false so
the bridge-only AuthService works. Missing/short keys still fail closed;
bridge + OPENBOT_SINGLE_USER/OPENBOT_DEV_NO_AUTH refuses (no shared
dev admin); ordinary OAuth/org behaviour is unchanged.

createRequestActor's getSession reads auth.api.getSession, so the
Copilot runtime identifyUser/identifyActor seam and the http-server
websocket guard see the same principal with no second change.

Security properties (reviewed, deterministic):
  - HMAC-SHA256 with timingSafeEqual; 60s TTL; single-use nonces;
    role allowlist admin|user; key >=32 chars or the bridge stays inert.
  - No cookie forge: the bridge never reads/writes BetterAuth cookies.
  - No shared admin: no static user, no OPENBOT_SINGLE_USER change, no
    first-visitor promotion; role comes from the home allowlist only.
  - No phone user_id trust: the id is the home-mapped upstream id inside
    the signed assertion, never a request body field.
  - Private listener only: refuses unless the assertion key is configured,
    and the home proxy only forwards to loopback/compose addresses.
